## File Naming and Organization

- Use PascalCase for React components (e.g. `components/SmartChart/GraphHeader.tsx`)
- If a component can be used in many places, place it in the `components` folder
- Use kebab case for route directories if you add any (not currently present)
- Utility functions go in `src/utils/`
- TypeScript types that belong to a category (like "graph" or "survey") and don't relate to a specific file go in `src/types/`
- Custom hooks go in `src/hooks/`
- Static assets go in `public/` when they need to be fetched, or to `src/assets/` if they can be simply imported

## Static data types

- surveys_meta: metadata about each survey in format: ```{
    "id": "id",
    "weights": {
        "weightName": "weight_key" // May be 0 or more weights in this dictionary
    },
    "sectorFieldName": "sector_field_id", // optional
    "dataLink": "https://socsci4.tau.ac.il/mu2/ines/data/our-data/#carousel_ff67" // link for human users to the origin data that is available in the website
}```
- surveys_data: csv files with the surveys data
- question_items: arrays of question instances in the format: ```[
    {
        "id": "1. שאלה בעברית", // question id
        "questionHebrewDescription": "שאלה בעברית", // question hebrew description
        "questionSurveyId": "a1", // qis id: the question instance id, as written in the survey's stata file
        "type": "demography", // question type is "demography" or "category"
        "disabled": "true",
        "englishDescription": "respondent number" // english description of the question
    },
    ...
]```